.TH "ROARK\-INTEGRATIONS\-CALENDAR\-TARGET\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-integrations-calendar-target-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-integrations\-calendar\-target\-create \- Create a bookable target
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark integrations calendar target create
\fIconnection\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Only for a connection whose `capabilities.roarkOwnsBookingPolicy` is true. A calendar with no scheduling of its own has nothing an agent can be pointed at, so the thing a calendar tool books into is created here: the calendar, how long an appointment runs, and the hours it is offered in. The policy and the hours are written together, because a target with no hours offers nothing. Refused if the calendar is one the account can only read.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/integrations/calendar/{connectionId}/targets
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIconnection\-id\fR
Calendar connection ID
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Unique within the connection, and how a config file refers to this target. Letters, digits, spaces, _ or \-. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
The calendar to write appointments to, from `GET /v1/integrations/calendar/{connectionId}/calendars`. `primary` is accepted and stored as the account’s own id. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-buffer\-before\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
Dead time before an appointment, counted as busy when a slot is offered. Defaults to 0. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-buffer\-after\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-notice\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
How soon from now an appointment may be made. Defaults to 120. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-horizon\-days\fR \fI<value>\fR
How far ahead appointments may be made. Defaults to 30. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\-interval\-minutes\fR \fI<value>\fR
The grid slots are offered on. Defaults to the duration, which gives back\-to\-back appointments. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-day\-events\-block\fR
Whether an all\-day event closes the day. Defaults to true, because a calendar marks all\-day events free unless their creator says otherwise and a public holiday entered as one would otherwise be bookable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fI<value>\fR
The windows of the week appointments are offered in. Omit to adopt Monday to Friday, 09:00 to 17:00. A target with no windows offers nothing at all, which reads to a caller as a permanently full diary. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark integrations calendar target create <connection\-id> \-\-name <value> \-\-calendar\-id <value> \-\-duration\-minutes <value>
.fi
